{"timestamp": 1779397226.3665862, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 20, "data": {"caller": "player_3", "reason": "Diana reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "navigation", "victim_name": "Alice"}, {"room": "medbay", "victim_name": "Eve"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779397226.3671901, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 20, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779397243.005569, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I reported Eve's body in Medbay. I see Alice is dead too, but I never saw her body, so she must be somewhere else on the map. \n\nHere is my route: I started in Medbay, then went to Electrical, Security, Weapons, Cafeteria, and finally back to Medbay where I found Eve. \n\nDuring my rotation, I saw Bob and Frank quite a bit on the right side of the ship. Bob, you were around Security and Weapons. Frank, I saw you in Electrical and Security, and then I saw you leave Weapons heading towards Cafeteria right before I went down to Medbay. I haven't seen Charlie at all this round. \n\nFrank, did you pass by Medbay after Cafeteria? Bob and Frank can vouch for my whereabouts for most of the round. Let's hear where Charlie was and if anyone knows where Alice went down."}}
{"timestamp": 1779397273.0375092, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Hey everyone. To answer Diana \u2014 I was on the opposite side of the ship from you, which is why our paths never crossed. I started in Navigation, did some work there, then headed down through Storage to Lower Engine, up to Upper Engine, and was working my way around toward Oxygen. I saw Alice early on in Navigation around tick 8, she was coming from Security. That's the last I saw of her. After that I didn't run into anybody \u2014 the left and bottom side of the map was pretty empty.\n\nNow, something I want to flag, Diana: you said Frank left Weapons heading toward Cafeteria right before you went down to Medbay. Cafeteria connects directly to Medbay. That means Frank had a clean shot at slipping into Medbay through the Cafeteria corridor, killing Eve, and looping back before you got there. The timing lines up pretty tightly.\n\nAlso, Diana \u2014 you came from Cafeteria into Medbay yourself and \"found\" the body. I'm not accusing you outright, but reporters always need to be looked at, especially when the killer could be either the person who just came from Cafeteria OR the person who entered right after.\n\nFrank, I'd like to hear your exact route after Weapons. Did you go to Cafeteria and then where? Because if you went anywhere near Medbay, we have a problem."}}
{"timestamp": 1779397291.2070029, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Charlie, hold your horses. I didn't go anywhere near Medbay after Cafeteria. I went straight from Cafeteria to Oxygen to do my task, and Bob is literally in Oxygen with me right now at the time of the report. Bob, please back me up on that when you speak. \n\nHere is my exact route: Storage right at the start, passed through Medbay very early, then Electrical, Security, Weapons, Cafeteria, and finally Oxygen. \n\nI can confirm parts of Diana's story. I saw her in Security around tick 12 and then again in Weapons around 16, so her path checks out for the middle of the round. I also saw Bob in Electrical early on before we eventually met up in Oxygen at the end. \n\nCharlie, you're trying to throw suspicion on me, but your own story has some massive red flags. You admit you were the last person to see Alice in Navigation around tick 8, and now she's dead. You also claim you were working your way up the left side toward Oxygen... but Bob and I are in Oxygen right now, and you aren't here. You had free rein on the bottom and left side of the map where Alice disappeared, and Upper Engine connects directly to Medbay as well, meaning you could have easily dropped Eve.\n\nBob, you have the final word. Confirm our Oxygen alibi, and let me know what you think about Charlie. I think he just outed himself as Alice's killer."}}
{"timestamp": 1779397308.702933, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Alright everyone, I have the final pieces of the puzzle, and they completely blow Charlie's theory out of the water. \n\nFirst, Frank \u2014 yes, I can 100% vouch for you. I saw you in Electrical early on (around ticks 8 and 9), and I saw you walk directly into Oxygen from Cafeteria at tick 20, literally right as this meeting was called. There is zero physical way you had time to go down to Medbay, kill Eve, and bounce back up to Oxygen. You are completely cleared for Eve's death.\n\nDiana, your route also checks out perfectly with my observations. I was tracking right alongside your path: I saw you leave Medbay for Electrical early on (tick 4), move to Security (tick 8), and I was in Weapons with you around ticks 13 through 15. \n\nCharlie, that leaves you. You tried to throw suspicion onto Frank for Eve's death, but his alibi is completely rock solid because of me. Meanwhile, you freely admit you were the last person to see Alice alive at tick 8 down in Navigation, and now she's dead. You also claim you were working your way up to Oxygen... but I've been around the top of the map and ended in Oxygen, and you are nowhere to be found. \n\nSince there's only one Duck, and Frank and Diana both have verified paths and alibis that cross-reference with mine, it has to be Charlie. He killed Alice down in Navigation/Lower Engine, then probably rotated up to Medbay to kill Eve before Diana found the body. \n\nWe have four players left and one Duck. Vote Charlie and we win this."}}
{"timestamp": 1779397317.346957, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Charlie"}}
{"timestamp": 1779397364.5885482, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Hold on, everyone. Before you all vote me out, take a hard look at what just happened in this meeting. Bob, you're suspiciously precise. You claim you tracked Diana's exact ticks \u2014 leaving Medbay at 4, Security at 8, Weapons 13 to 15 \u2014 AND you were in Electrical with Frank early on AND you ended in Oxygen. That's a player who has apparently witnessed everyone but somehow done zero tasks. The task counter barely moved. Where are your tasks, Bob?\n\nSecond, Frank and Bob are alibi-ing each other in Oxygen. Classic Duck-and-Goose pairing where one Duck builds a clean story with a Goose who genuinely was there \u2014 except we only have Bob's word that Frank walked in \"right as the meeting was called.\" If Frank actually slipped down through Cafeteria-Medbay-Cafeteria-Oxygen, Bob in Oxygen would only see him arrive \u2014 he wouldn't know where Frank actually came from.\n\nOn me being on the left side: yes, I was rotating up through Storage and the engines. I did briefly cut through Medbay on my way around \u2014 early, well before tick 15 \u2014 and Eve wasn't there at that time. After that I went Electrical and Security to keep ticking tasks. I didn't loop back down to Medbay. The reason Bob didn't see me up top is the same reason I didn't see him \u2014 we were on offset rotations.\n\nAnd Diana \u2014 you reported the body. You came in from Cafeteria. Frank also came through Cafeteria. The kill window is between you two, not me from across the map.\n\nI think the real play here is Frank. Bob, I'm not saying you're lying on purpose \u2014 I'm saying Frank used your presence in Oxygen as cover. Don't lock this in on me when the timing on Frank is the tightest."}}
{"timestamp": 1779397388.143656, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Charlie, you just caught yourself in a massive lie. Stop and listen to what you just said. \n\nIn your very first speech, you explicitly claimed your route was Navigation, down through Storage to Lower Engine, up to Upper Engine, and then toward Oxygen. You literally said: \"After that I didn't run into anybody \u2014 the left and bottom side of the map was pretty empty.\" \n\nNow, in your panic after Bob cleared me, you've completely changed your story! Suddenly you're claiming you cut through Medbay, then went to Electrical and Security to do tasks? If you were in Electrical and Security, you would have run into me, Diana, or Bob, because we were all rotating through those exact rooms mid-round. \n\nYou changed your entire route just to try and scramble for an alibi after Bob dismantled your first one. You admit you were the last to see Alice, and now you're openly contradicting your own path. \n\nBob, Diana, Charlie is 100% the Duck. His story is falling apart. Let's vote him out and win this."}}
{"timestamp": 1779397402.0711858, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Frank hit the nail right on the head. Charlie, you completely panicked and changed your entire story. In your first speech, you explicitly stated you were on the left side of the map\u2014Lower Engine, Upper Engine, heading to Oxygen\u2014and that you didn't see anyone. When I proved you couldn't have been heading to Oxygen because I was there and you weren't, you suddenly changed your route to Medbay, Electrical, and Security! \n\nIf you had actually been in Electrical or Security mid-round, Diana, Frank, or I would have definitely seen you because we were all rotating through those exact rooms. You got caught in a lie and tried to rewrite your path to save yourself, but you just dug your own grave. \n\nMy observations of Frank and Diana are exactly as I stated before, and they are rock solid. Charlie is the last Duck. Let's finish this and win.\n\nCharlie"}}
